  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tripartite constituents effectively address working condition challenges in different forms of employment in line with ILS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">China is pursuing high-quality development with a people-centered approach, making progress toward common prosperity. However, challenges such as unbalanced development and the growing needs of the people persist.

Megatrends like digitalization, technological upgrades, the platform economy&apos;s growth, and demographic changes require adjustments in the regulation and governance of working conditions and labour relations. These adjustments address new forms of employment, income inequality, and protections for workers with family responsibilities.

Collective bargaining and labour market institutions are crucial for managing technical, economic, and social transformations. Tripartite constituents and partners in China are exploring effective regulations to protect workers&apos; rights and well-being while promoting productivity and economic growth. Efforts are underway to improve labour laws and institutions to support high-quality employment, protect platform workers, and promote a family-friendly society.

The Country Outcome Programme CHN156 supports the government and social partners in enhancing policies to narrow income disparities, improve working conditions, promote harmonious labour relations, and support workers with family responsibilities. Key outputs include:

1) Research on working hours and arrangements in China, shared through consultations and seminars.

2) Analysis of international experiences with flexible working time and condition regulations.

3) Research on digitalization&apos;s impact on working conditions in China.

4) Translation of the Global Wage Flagship Report 2024 and follow-up discussions with stakeholders.

5) Dissemination of good practices in skill-based collective negotiation for effective wage negotiations.

6) Technical support to enhance capacity for addressing work-life balance challenges and creating family-friendly working conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
